title: Payers › History & Changes › Workflow versions
route: /payers/summit?tab=history
intro: Every save of a draft, publish, archive and restore of this payer's workflows is a version row, newest first: the workflow's name, the version number, its status (Draft, Published, Archived), who did it, when (demo time) and why. A row opens that exact version in a right-hand panel (read only, with its path) and can be restored as a draft. Restoring never touches the published version: the draft is checked and published like any other, so new cases keep matching the published one until then. A case keeps the version it started with.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open History & Changes\nclick 'Workflow versions' (closed, with a one-line summary)"
screen sm "Closed: '4 saved versions, newest first.\nLatest: Summit Initial Authorization, Residential SUD (copy), version 1, Tue 10:42 am.'"
screen ls "Open: one row per version, newest first\nWorkflow name, 'version 1', status pill,\n'Jordan Perez · Tue 10:42 am · Reason: Ready for Summit initial requests'\nButtons 'View' and 'Restore as draft'"
decision dm "More than one workflow?"
input fl "Pick 'Workflow'\nAll workflows or one"
process fl2 "List shows that workflow's versions only"
decision de "Any version saved yet?"
screen em "'No saved versions yet'\nEvery save, publish, archive and restore of a workflow is listed here\nwith who, when and why."
process sd "Seeded rows read 'Made from the Process tab'\n(the earlier process, migrated)\nor 'Sample workflow from the starter template'"

group gW "Where rows come from (Workflow Builder)"
  store w1 "Save draft: one draft row per version\n(a newer save replaces the earlier draft row)"
  store w2 "Publish with a reason: the draft row becomes a Published row"
  store w3 "Archive: an Archived row"
  store w4 "Restore as draft: a new Draft row\n'Restored from version 1'"
endgroup

click vw "Click 'View'"
overlay pn "Version panel (right-hand)\nThe read-only canvas for that version\n'Open in Workflow Builder' at the foot"
click xc "Press Escape or click the X"
process xc2 "Panel closes; the list is as it was"
click rs "Click 'Restore as draft'"
store rd "A draft of the next version is made from that version\nThe published version keeps matching new cases\nEdit audit gets a 'Workflow' line"
toast tr "'Restored as a draft'\n'Summit process (migrated) version 1 is now draft version 2.\nThe published version has not changed.'"
process nr "A new row at the top: 'Restored from version 1', Draft"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Read a workflow"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Save a draft and publish"
goto g3 "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Edit audit"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Workflow › Match and pin the payer workflow"
process pin "A case keeps the version it started with\nPublishing a newer version moves nobody"
end e1 "Person can see who changed which version, and why, and bring one back as a draft"

s1 --> sm --> ls --> dm
dm -->|Yes| fl --> fl2 --> de
dm -->|No| de
de -->|No| em
de -->|Yes| sd --> vw
ls -.-> w1 & w2 & w3 & w4
w2 -.-> g2
vw --> pn --> xc --> xc2
pn -.-> g1
sd --> rs --> rd --> tr --> nr --> e1
rd -.-> g3
nr -.-> pin --> g4
